.TH PERMPROBE 1
.SH NAME
permprobe \- exercise SmallOS credential and permission behavior
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B permprobe
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B permprobe
is a regression probe for the SmallOS kernel permission model. It verifies
root credentials, kernel-owned umask handling, file creation modes, non-root
read/write/access denials, owner-only chmod, root-only chown, and cleanup of
temporary ext2 paths.
.PP
The probe is installed under
.I /usr/libexec/tests
and is normally run by the shell selftest and host ELF regression harness.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 when every check passes, or 1 after printing failed check names.
